  "notes": {
   "4...Nd7": "Preparing ...Ngf6: if White exchanges on f6, Black takes back with the knight.",
   "5.Nf3": "White develops.",
   "5...Ngf6": "Now the knight challenges the e4 knight.",
   "6.Nxf6+": "White exchanges.",
   "6...Nxf6": "Black recaptures with a piece and keeps a healthy pawn structure."
  },
  "explanation": "The Karpov Variation is a small but important idea: by putting a knight on d7 first, Black can meet an exchange on f6 by recapturing with the other knight. Black keeps a healthy pawn structure and a solid position.",
